          "type": "heading",
          "text": "5. Why Limit Fan-Out",
          "ink": "red"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Unbounded fan-out exhausts sockets: `EMFILE`, `ECONNRESET`.",
            "It also drains DB pools, memory, and triggers 429s.",
            "==Little's Law==: in-flight ≈ arrival rate × latency.",
            "Stay under `maxSockets`, pool max, and threadpool size."
          ],
          "style": "cross"
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "6. Rolling Worker Pool",
          "ink": "blue"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "let i = 0;",
            "const worker = async () => {",
            "  while (i < items.length)",
            "    await task(items[i++]);",
            "};",
            "await Promise.all(pool.map(worker));"
          ],
          "note": "pool = N slots, shared cursor"
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Batch vs rolling pool",
          "text": "Chunks of N with `Promise.all` stall on the **slowest** item per batch; a rolling pool keeps N in flight the whole time."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "7. p-limit Takes Thunks",
          "ink": "green"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "js",
          "lines": [
            "const limit = pLimit(5);",
            "await Promise.all(items.map(i =>",
            "  limit(() => fetchOne(i))));",
            "// WRONG: limit(fetchOne(i))"
          ],
          "note": "wrap a thunk, not a promise"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
